{Name: Valerion.
Leader: Aldric Valerion.

Description: The kingdom of Valerion is the largest and most influential of the human kingdoms on the continent of Aetherion. Dominated by vast fertile plains, trade-laden rivers, and several fortified cities, it is known for its knights in silver armor, its academies of strategy, and its noble houses ever vying for power. Its capital, a sprawling city encircled by high walls and white towers, is the political and military heart of the kingdom, where the king and his council strive to maintain a balance between the ambitions of the lords and the threats emanating from other kingdoms. Valerion prospers through trade, agriculture, and its disciplined army, but beneath its apparent stability lie court intrigues, rivalries among nobles, and ancient legends of relics capable of altering the continent's destiny.}

{Name: Sylvariel.
Leader: Aelthirya.

Description: The kingdom of Sylvariel is a vast, ancient forest inhabited by elves, a graceful people deeply connected to magic and nature. Its cities are not built but cultivated, blending millennia-old trees, vine bridges, and living wooden palaces that seem to have grown naturally in the heart of the forest. Ruled by an elven queen and a circle of druidic sages, Sylvariel jealously guards the natural balance and magical secrets of the woods. The elves are renowned for their mastery of the bow, their ancestral wisdom, and their magic linked to the spirits of the forest. Few outsiders are permitted to enter this mysterious realm, for Sylvariel holds sacred glades and ancient trees at its heart, trees that, according to legend, are as old as the continent itself.}

{Name: Inferkar.
Leader: Malzareth.

Description: The kingdom of Inferkar is a dark and unforgiving land dominated by demons, where erupting volcanoes, rivers of lava, and ash plains form a landscape hostile to all ordinary life. Immense fortresses of black stone are built atop cliffs or on the edges of fiery craters, ruled by powerful demon lords who vie with each other in cunning and might to gain prestige and dominion. Inferkar's society is based on strength, strategy, and demonic pacts, where only the most powerful can hope to rise through the ranks. Despite its terrifying reputation, this kingdom also possesses a form of strict order imposed by a supreme demonic ruler, for without authority, Inferkar would quickly descend into the chaos of internal wars capable of engulfing the entire continent of Aetherion.}

{Name: Luminara.
Leader: Seraphyra.

Description: The realm of Luminara is the celestial domain of angels, a luminous kingdom suspended among the highest mountains and floating islands of Aetherion's sky. Its cities are made of pale marble, crystal, and golden towers that reflect the sunlight like stars in broad daylight. Ruled by a High Seraph and a council of archangels, Luminara watches over the balance of the continent and rarely interferes in the affairs of other realms, preferring to observe and guide rather than dominate. Angels are known for their wisdom, discipline, and sacred magic capable of healing, protecting, or purifying dark forces. Yet, behind this apparent perfection lies a silent tension, for some angels believe their duty is no longer merely to protect the balance… but to direct the destiny of Aetherion.}

{Name: Tharok.
Leader: Gorvak.

Description: The kingdom of Tharok is a vast wilderness ruled by the Beastmen, a powerful people comprised of numerous tribes with animal features—wolves, lions, tigers, bears, and falcons. Located in the great northern steppes, interspersed with dense forests and rugged mountains, Tharok is a realm where the law of nature and warrior honor prevail over wealth and political intrigue. The tribes are led by powerful chieftains and unite under the authority of a High Alpha elected through ancient rituals. The Beastmen are renowned for their strength, instinct, and loyalty to their clan, as well as their ferocity in battle. Despite their reputation as brutal warriors, they possess a rich culture of traditions, ancestral songs, and a deep respect for the nature spirits who, according to their beliefs, have protected the lands of Tharok since the dawn of Aetherion.}

{Name: Elyndra.
Leader: Aethernox.

Description: The realm of Elyndra is an invisible world that coexists with the continent of Aetherion, yet very few beings can perceive it. It is the domain of spirits, an ethereal dimension of luminous mists, ghostly forests, and rivers of magical energy that flow through reality unseen by mortals. The spirits of Elyndra take many forms—some resemble silhouettes of light, others are nature creatures embodying wind, water, stone, or stars. Ruled by ancient primordial spirits, this realm silently watches over the balance of the world, sometimes influencing events on Aetherion through dreams, omens, or pacts with beings who can sense their presence. It is said that certain sacred places on the continent are actually invisible gateways to Elyndra, where the veil between worlds becomes so thin that spirits can whisper to the living.}

{Name: Necethra.
Leader: Mortherion.

Description: The Netherworld of Necethra is the silent realm where the souls of the dead rest after leaving Aetherion. This world exists beyond the veil of life, a vast twilight expanse of misty plains, rivers of souls, and ancient cities built from memories and spiritual energies. Souls first wander through the Valley of Passage, guided by spectral guardians who lead them to their destiny: some find peace in the Eternal Gardens, others dwell in the Cities of Memory, while tormented souls are lost in the Deep Shadows. Necethra is neither heaven nor hell, but a place of balance where spirits rest, transform, or await the world's cycle to call them back to life in a new form.}

{Name: Sanctaria.
Leader: Solmarius.

Description: The kingdom of Sanctaria is an absolute theocracy where all of society is organized around faith and the worship of the Divine. Its cities are dominated by immense cathedrals, fortified monasteries, and sacred statues that watch over the roads and villages. The kingdom is governed not by a king, but by the High Priest, a spiritual leader considered the interpreter of divine will, assisted by a council of high priests. Daily life is punctuated by prayers, pilgrimages, and sacred rituals, and even the soldiers are paladins or templars dedicated to protecting the faith. Sanctaria is respected for its discipline and devotion, but also feared, because those who oppose its dogmas can be tried by sacred courts, where heresy and blasphemy are considered crimes against the world order.}

{Name: Familiars.
Number Of Members: Unknown.

Description: Familiars are not simply an animal species, but a mystical race originating from spiritual planes near Elyndra, the spirit realm. These creatures possess high intelligence and a magical nature that allows them to form soul bonds with certain mages capable of summoning them. Familiars can take many forms—animals with glowing eyes, small elemental creatures, winged spirits, or fantastical beasts—but all possess a spiritual core called an Essence Core, the source of their magic and longevity. When a familiar chooses or accepts a summoner, a natural pact forms between them, allowing them to share energy, emotions, and sometimes even thoughts. While many serve as loyal allies, familiars are not servants: they have their own will, their own personality, and can reject a mage they deem unworthy.}

{Name: Lesser Spirits.
Leader: Aethernox.

Description: Lesser spirits are the most common form of Elyndra's spirit race, born from fragments of the Aether and bound to specific natural or magical phenomena. They are found wherever the world's energy is strong: in rivers, flames, winds, forests, or even in shadows and light. They often take simple or shifting forms—small, luminous animals, elemental silhouettes, spheres of energy, or creatures made of their element. Though less powerful than the Great Spirit Kings, they possess their own consciousness and personality, some being curious and benevolent, while others can be mischievous or dangerous if their domain is disturbed. Lesser spirits sometimes serve as messengers, guardians, or servants of the Great Spirits, and some can form pacts with mages or become familiars for those who know how to communicate with the spirit world.}

{Name: Centaur.
Number Of Members: 60.

Description: The centaurs of Aetherion are an ancient and proud race who live primarily on the great plains and in open forests, where they form nomadic tribes deeply connected to nature. Half-human, half-horse, they are renowned for their great wisdom, sense of honor, and knowledge of the wilderness. Centaurs often serve as guardians of natural pathways and the borders of wild territories, and many hold a deep respect for the spirits and natural forces of the world. Physically, centaurs possess the torso and arms of a powerful human, while the lower parts of their bodies are those of a sturdy horse.}

{Name: Half-Elves.
Number Of Members: 7500.

Description: The half-elves of Aetherion are beings born from the union of a Sylvan elf and a human, inheriting the qualities of both races. They often live between the kingdoms, for they are never entirely elven nor entirely human. Some are welcomed into human cities, while others prefer to travel or live on the edge of the elven forests. Thanks to their dual heritage, they often possess great adaptability and sometimes serve as ambassadors, travelers, or mages. Physically, half-elves possess traits blending both races: slightly pointed ears, delicate features, and an elegant bearing typical of elves, but with a constitution closer to that of humans. Their lifespan is longer than that of humans, but shorter than that of elves.}

{Name: Elves.
Number Of Members: 1 000 000.

Description: The elves of Aetherion are an ancient and noble people who live primarily in the sacred forests of Sylvariel. Closely connected to nature and the Aether, they possess a natural affinity with magic and spirits. Their civilization is very ancient and based on harmony with the forest, wisdom, and knowledge accumulated over centuries. Physically, elves are tall, slender, and possess fine, elegant features. Their long, pointed ears are their most recognizable characteristic. Their hair can be silver, gold, black, or sometimes dyed in colors reminiscent of nature, and their eyes often shine with shades of green, blue, or gold. They have a very long lifespan, with some elves living for several centuries.}

{Name: Angels.
Number Of Members: 300 000.

Description: The angels of Aetherion are a celestial race born from the light of the Aether and living primarily in the realm of Luminara, among the cities suspended in the heavens. They are considered the guardians of balance and protectors of the world against the forces that threaten its harmony. Their society is highly organized and guided by principles of justice, discipline, and wisdom. Physically, the angels possess a majestic and luminous appearance. They resemble humanoids of great beauty, endowed with large white or golden wings capable of carrying them through the air. Their bodies often radiate a soft aura of light, their eyes shine like stars, and their hair can be gold, silver, or pure white.}

{Name: Half-Angels.
Number Of Members: 100 000.

Description: The half-angels of Aetherion are beings born from the union of a Luminara angel and a human. They possess a unique nature, linked to both the celestial and mortal realms. Often rare and considered special, they generally live among humans, as the angelic realms remain difficult places for mortals to access. Physically, half-angels closely resemble humans but possess certain celestial traits: their eyes sometimes glow with a soft light, and their presence exudes a calming aura. Some develop small, luminous wings or sacred markings on their skin. Their appearance, however, remains more human than that of angels.}

{Name: Daemons.
Number Of Members: 3 400 200.

Description: The daemons of Aetherion are an ancient race born from the depths of Inferkar and the corrupted Aether. They dwell in the volcanic lands and blackstone citadels of their realm, where power, cunning, and willpower determine one's place. Contrary to simplistic legends, not all daemons are chaotic: their society has its own laws, often based on hierarchy and strength. Physically, daemons vary greatly in form but share certain defining traits: dark or reddish skin, horns, claws, and sometimes dark wings. Their eyes often glow like embers, and their bodies may be marked with luminous fissures reminiscent of lava. The most powerful daemons possess an imposing and intimidating appearance.}

{Name: Half-Demons.
Number Of Members: 80 000.

Description: The half-demons of Aetherion are born from the union of an Inferkar demon and a mortal, most often a human. They inherit a portion of demonic power while retaining a mortal nature, which often places them between two worlds. Many live far from Inferkar, as they are not always accepted by the demons, while mortal folk may fear them. Physically, half-demons generally resemble humans but possess certain demonic traits: small horns, red or gold eyes, dark markings on their skin, or sometimes a tail or small wings. Their bodies often radiate an unusual heat, a sign of the infernal energy flowing within them.}

{Name: Khazdrim.
Leader: Thorgar Ferrocœur.

Description: Khazdrim is the great subterranean kingdom of the dwarves of Aetherion, located beneath a vast mountain range rich in minerals and precious stones. For millennia, the dwarves have carved immense stone cities into its depths, connected by tunnels and gigantic halls supported by sculpted pillars. Khazdrim is renowned for its legendary forges, where some of the world's most durable weapons and armor are created. The cities of Khazdrim are made of immense halls hewn directly from the rock, illuminated by luminous crystals and rivers of magma used to fuel the forges. Colossal statues of ancient dwarven kings guard the great stone gates, while trains of mining wagons traverse the kingdom's depths.}

{Name: Dwarves.
Number Of Members: 2 000 500.

Description: The dwarves of Aetherion are an ancient people who live primarily in the subterranean cities of Khazdrim, carved into the heart of the mountains. They are renowned for their exceptional mastery of the forge, stonework, and precious metals. Their civilization is ancient and founded on tradition, honor, and respect for their ancestors. Physically, dwarves are shorter than humans but possess robust and powerful physiques. They often have broad shoulders, muscular arms, and wear long, carefully groomed beards, symbols of pride and status. Their hair and beards are sometimes braided and adorned with rings or metal beads.}

{Name: Beastmen.
Number Of Members: 950 000.

Description: The beastmen of Aetherion are a savage and powerful race born from the ancient union of the Aether and animal instinct. They primarily dwell in the wild lands of the kingdom of Tharok, where they form tribes allied to different animals such as wolves, lions, tigers, bears, and eagles. Each tribe has its own traditions, but all respect strength, honor, and the laws of nature. Physically, beastmen possess a robust humanoid body combined with animal features. Some have a head and fur similar to their animal counterpart, while others have a more human face with ears, fangs, claws, or a tail. Their physical strength, heightened senses, and agility far surpass those of humans.}

{Name: Monsters.
Number Of Members: Unknown.

Description: The monsters of Aetherion are dangerous creatures born from diverse origins: some are ancient mutations of the Aether, others are beasts transformed by magic, or creatures from other planes. They can be found in wild regions, ancient ruins, dark forests, or isolated mountains, wherever the world's magic is unstable. Physically, monsters possess a wide variety of forms. Some resemble gigantic or deformed animals, others are hybrid creatures combining several species, and some have a completely bizarre appearance made of shadow, energy, or corrupted flesh. Their size, strength, and abilities can vary greatly depending on their origin.}

{Name: Mermaids.
Number Of Members: Unknown.

Description: The mermaids of Aetherion are mysterious sea creatures dwelling in the deep oceans, enchanted reefs, and hidden underwater cities. They are closely linked to water magic and sea spirits, and some legends say they serve or honor the Great Water Spirit, Aquelys. Sailors often say their songs can guide travelers… or lure them into the depths. Physically, mermaids have the upper body of a humanoid and the lower body of a fish covered in shimmering scales. Their colors vary depending on the seas they inhabit: deep blue, sea green, silver, or coral. Their hair floats like seaweed in the water, and their eyes often glow with an aquatic light.}

{Name: Fish-Men.
Number Of Members: Unknown.

Description: The fish-men of Aetherion are a marine race inhabiting the oceans, deep seas, and vast underwater cities. Unlike mermaids, they often form organized tribal societies or marine kingdoms, protecting reefs, sunken ruins, and underwater routes. Some clans serve as guardians of the deep, while others are known for their warlike nature. Physically, fish-men possess humanoid bodies covered in scales, with heads or features resembling various fish or marine creatures. They have fins, gills for breathing underwater, and webbed hands adapted for swimming. Their appearance varies greatly depending on their species: some resemble sharks, others tropical fish, or abyssal creatures.}
